Potential TS issue: `this.formulario.controls.codigoPostal.valid` — good. `telefono10(this.formulario.controls.telefonoNuevo)` accepts AbstractControl; FormControl extends; fine.

`lineas.at(0)?.setValue` returns void; fine.

`WritableSignal` import from @angular/core exists. Good.

`cliente` type: existente is ClienteVenta | undefined; `existente ?? {...}` type ClienteVenta. Good.

Now HTML. Need ensure form controls nested properly. Use `<form [formGroup]="formulario" (ngSubmit)="finalizar()">` wrapping all steps; buttons type button except final submit.

Step indicator:
```
<ol class="pasos">
 @for (paso of [1,2,3,4]; track paso) { <li [class...]> ... </li> }
</ol>
```
Use inline array in template `@for (numero of [1, 2, 3, 4]; track numero)` allowed? Yes, array literal in template expression works.

Step 1:
```
@if (paso()===1) {
 <div class="opciones">
  <label><input type="radio" formControlName="clienteTipo" value="EXISTENTE" (change)="intentoPaso.set(false)"> Cliente existente</label>
 ...
 </div>
 @if (formulario.controls.clienteTipo.value==='EXISTENTE') { <label class=campo>Cliente<select formControlName="clienteId"> <option [value]="0">Selecciona...</option> @for... <option [value]="cliente.id">...</option> } }
 @else { new fields }
}
```
Note `formControlName="clienteId"` with number control and `<option [value]="cliente.id">` — Angular selects option by value string; with `[value]` number, SelectControlValueAccessor uses `value` property and compares via `String()`? It should work; to be safe use `[ngValue]="cliente.id"`. Since ReactiveFormsModule provides `NgSelectOption` with ngValue. Use `[ngValue]="cliente.id"`. Need ensure `option [ngValue]` works without FormsModule? `NgSelectOption` is part of ReactiveFormsModule exports? Actually `NgSelectOption` is declared in `SelectControlValueAccessor` module and exported by both FormsModule and ReactiveFormsModule. Yes.

Step 2 table:
```
<div formArrayName="lineas">
 @for (linea of lineas.controls; track $index; let indice=$index) {
  <div class="fila-linea" [formGroupName]="indice">
   <label class=campo>SKU<select formControlName="sku" (change)="sincronizarLineas()">... 
```
Wait `sincronizarLineas` is private; template can't call private. Need make it protected. Change in TS: `protected sincronizarLineas()`. Also `contexto()` private used only in TS; fine. `validarPaso` private used only TS. Let's edit `private sincronizarLineas` to protected.

