```
Note `lineasCarrito()[indice]?.subtotal` — array index returns LineaCarrito (not undefined under TS noUncheckedIndexedAccess maybe false), but Angular template null-safe okay.

Step 3 fields with `(input)="alCambiarCp($event)"` on codigoPostal. `requiereFactura` checkbox with `(change)="alCambiarCheckbox($event, requiereFactura)"`.
Show tarifa note:
```
@if (tarifa(); as t) { Tarifa Local León: $200.00 · 2 días } @else { <p class="error">Sin cobertura...</p> }
```
Step 4: coupon input, buttons, checkbox primera compra, method radios/select, estadoPago radios, ultimos4 if TARJETA, summary card with subtotal/descuento/envío/total.

Navigation buttons at bottom:
```
@if (paso()>1) { <button (click)="retroceder()">Anterior</button> }
@if (paso()<4) { <button (click)="avanzar()">Continuar</button> } @else { <button type="submit" (click)="finalizar()">Registrar venta</button> }
```
But form has `(ngSubmit)="finalizar()"`, so submit button with type submit suffices; avoid double call by not adding click. Use `<button type="submit" class="boton primario">Registrar venta</button>`. However `finalizar` called on ngSubmit; good.

`@if (intentoPaso()) { <p class=error-paso>...</p> }` at bottom.

Note about no access for new client, no PAN/CVV.

Let's write.

I used `telefonoInvalido()` and `esRfcInvalido()` methods not yet defined in TS. Need add them. Also check `descuento.valor + '%'` in template — descuento.valor is number, `+` with string works in Angular expression? Angular template expression supports `+` for string concatenation if one operand string; but number + string yields string? In JS, `10 + '%'` = '10%'. Angular expression parser follows JS semantics mostly. Should be okay. But to be safe use interpolation pieces: `{{ descuento.valor }}%` and `{{ '$' + descuento.valor }}`. Let's adjust later.

Add methods:
