Now the form page. This is the most complex. Let me write TS carefully.

Imports:
- Component, computed, inject, signal
- FormBuilder, FormArray, ReactiveFormsModule, Validators, ValidatorFn, AbstractControl, ValidationErrors
- ActivatedRoute, Router, RouterLink
- CurrencyPipe maybe for preview prices
- AvisosServicio
- IMAGENES_DISPONIBLES, COLORES_PRODUCTO, TALLAS_PRODUCTO
- NavegacionProductos
- ProductosServicio
- types

Need `takeUntilDestroyed` from `@angular/core/rxjs-interop`.

Let me define the validator outside the class:

```ts
const seleccionesRequeridas: ValidatorFn = (control: AbstractControl): ValidationErrors | null => {
  const colores = control.get('colores');
  const tallas = control.get('tallas');
  if (!(colores instanceof FormArray) || !(tallas instanceof FormArray)) {
    return null;
  }
  const hayColor = colores.controls.some((item) => item.value === true);
  const hayTalla = tallas.controls.some((item) => item.value === true && item.enabled);
  const errores: ValidationErrors = {};
  if (!hayColor) errores['sinColor'] = true;
  if (!hayTalla) errores['sinTalla'] = true;
  return Object.keys(errores).length > 0 ? errores : null;
};
```
Careful with `noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature` — using bracket assignment on ValidationErrors (index signature) is fine.

Form:
```ts
private readonly fb = inject(FormBuilder);
...
protected readonly idEditar = this.ruta.snapshot.paramMap.get('id');
protected readonly producto = this.idEditar === null ? undefined : this.servicio.obtenerProducto(Number(this.idEditar));
protected readonly esEdicion = this.producto !== undefined;

protected readonly forma = this.fb.nonNullable.group(
  {
    nombre: [this.producto?.nombre ?? '', [Validators.required, Validators.minLength(3), Validators.maxLength(60)]],
    categoriaId: [this.producto?.categoriaId ?? 1, Validators.required],
    descripcion: [this.producto?.descripcion ?? ''],
    composicionTextil: [this.producto?.composicionTextil ?? ''],
    guiaMedidas: [this.producto?.guiaMedidas ?? ''],
    precioVenta: [this.producto?.precioVenta ?? 0, [Validators.required, Validators.min(1)]],
    permiteBajoPedido: [this.producto?.permiteBajoPedido ?? true],
    colores: this.fb.nonNullable.array(
      COLORES_PRODUCTO.map((color) => [this.producto?.colores.includes(color.codigo) ?? false]),
    ),
    tallas: this.fb.nonNullable.array(
      TALLAS_PRODUCTO.map((talla) => [this.producto?.tallas.includes(talla.codigo) ?? false]),
    ),
    imagenGeneral: [this.producto?.imagenes.find((i)=>i.color===null)?.url ?? ''],
    imagenesPorColor: this.fb.nonNullable.group(
      Object.fromEntries(COLORES_PRODUCTO.map(c => [c.codigo, [this.producto?.imagenes.find(i=>i.color===c.codigo)?.url ?? '']]))
    ),
    stockMinimo: [5, [Validators.required, Validators.min(0)]],
    cantidadReposicion: [20, [Validators.required, Validators.min(1)]],
  },
  { validators: seleccionesRequeridas },
);
```

Type issue: `Object.fromEntries` returns `{ [k: string]: string[] }`, passing to `fb.group` may infer index signature; `this.forma.controls.imagenesPorColor.controls['NG']` would be typed as AbstractControl<any> maybe. With `noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature`, bracket access is required. To avoid complexity, define explicit group:

